LightGBM regressor (num_leaves=127, learning_rate=0.08). Tabular coordinate regression strongly favors decision trees, and depth-wise XGBoost with exact second-order regularization provides diverse and complementary decision partitions to LightGBM's best-first leaf-wise growth. Both models are configured to consume identical tabular feature representations and output continuous 1D float32 fare prediction arrays.", "training_evaluation": "Eliminate the PyTorch DataLoader and StandardScaler pipeline, training LightGBM and GPU XGBoost directly on the unscaled 12M-row tabular features with early stopping against the 250,000-sample holdout validation set. Evaluate both models on the holdout validation split and perform a grid search over convex blending weights w in [0, 1] to minimize validation RMSE. Generate blended predictions for test.csv, enforce statutory minimum fare clipping at $2.50, save to ./submission/submission.csv matching sample_submission.csv format, verify all integrity assertions (9,914 rows, no NaNs), and log the Final Validation Score."}, "parse_success": true, "raw_response": "{
