atBoostRegressor with iterations=1600, learning_rate=0.08, depth=8, loss_function='RMSE', task_type='GPU', random_seed=42) alongside leaf-wise LightGBM and depth-wise GPU XGBoost. Spatial fare estimation benefits significantly from structural ensemble diversity; CatBoost's oblivious symmetric trees offer distinct inductive biases and built-in regularizations that produce decorrelated residual errors compared to LightGBM's leaf-wise splits and XGBoost's depth-wise splits. Configure all three estimators to consume identical unscaled float32 tabular feature matrices and output continuous 1D float32 fare prediction arrays. Maintain identical loss objectives (RMSE on raw fare_amount) and reproducible random seeds (42) across all models.", "training_evaluation": "Sequentially train LightGBM, GPU XGBoost, and GPU CatBoost on the 28M-row dataset with early stopping against the 250,000-sample holdout validation set, running explicit garbage collection (gc.collect()) between model fits to guarantee GPU and system memory safety. Perform a fine-grained grid search over 3D simplex blending weights (w1, w2, w3) summing to 1 on the holdout validation split to minimize validation RMSE. Generate blended predictions for test.csv, enforce NYC statutory minimum fare clipping at $2.50, and write the output directly to ./submission/submission.csv matching the sample_submission.csv schema. Verify all submission integrity assertions (9,914 rows, no NaNs or null values, correct column headers 'key' and 'fare_amount'), and print the Final Validation Score using the official competition metric."}, "parse_success": true, "raw_response": "{
