 maintain 25M train / 100k validation split sizes, and cast all newly derived features to float32 or int8.", "model_design": "WHAT: Scale LightGBM model capacity by updating default hyperparameters in build_lgbm_regressor to num_leaves=511, max_depth=10, and min_child_samples=100, while preserving learning_rate=0.08, n_estimators=2000, and regularization terms. WHY: LightGBM with 127 leaves lacked the representational capacity on 25 million records to partition high-dimensional geographic coordinates effectively, causing it to fall behind XGBoost's depth-9 architecture and receive 0.000 weight in the ensemble. HOW: In build_lgbm_regressor(), adjust the default_params dictionary to set num_leaves: 511, max_depth: 10, and min_child_samples: 100, aligning its spatial resolution capability with XGBoost and enabling genuine tripartite model complementarity during blending. Interface constraints: Retain the build_lgbm_regressor(params: Optional[Dict[str, Any]] = None) -> lgb.LGBMRegressor signature, returning a standard scikit-learn compatible estimator."}, "parse_success": true, "raw_response": "{
